# Daylight DC-1 (jagar) side buttons (mt6779-keypad matrix).
#
# The keypad's DT keymap emits KEY_F12 for the top-left "Quick Action" button
# and KEY_F11 for the bottom-right "Back Button" (a.k.a. Walkie Talkie) --
# Daylight's official names; stock Android assigns neither. F11/F12 collide
# with ordinary application function keys, so remap them to KEY_PROG1 and
# KEY_PROG2 (XF86Launch1/XF86Launch2), which nothing else emits and which
# GNOME Settings > Keyboard > Custom Shortcuts can capture by pressing the
# physical button. Default actions ship in 10-dc1-gnome.gschema.override.
#
# Match: the keypad's kernel modalias, udev's first evdev hwdb lookup
# (60-evdev.rules: `hwdb --subsystem=input --lookup-prefix=evdev:`), which
# needs no DMI data. The id block (bus 0019 host, all-zero vendor/product/
# version) is unique on this board -- the PMIC keys are v0001p0001e0001 --
# and the key-capability list stays behind the wildcard because this remap
# itself rewrites it.
#
# Scancodes read back from the device via EVIOCGKEYCODE (matrix row/column
# codes, verified 2026-08-20): 0 -> KEY_VOLUMEDOWN, 1 -> KEY_F11,
# 3 -> KEY_F12.
evdev:input:b0019v0000p0000e0000-e0,1,4,k*
 KEYBOARD_KEY_03=prog1
 KEYBOARD_KEY_01=prog2
